./arena
./array
./error

+ ScratchMark is Size

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Scratch'Item

` A growable stack of plain values whose finished runs are handed out as read-only spans. Storage
` lives in an Arena, so a span taken before the stack grows keeps reading the run it was taken
` from: the old buffer is never reused until the Arena is released. Slice only finished runs;
` writes go through the stack by index and land in the current storage.

_ items Array'Item'ArenaBacking
_ arena Arena
+ length Size = 0

────────────────────
+ This
    - arena Arena
    - capacity Size = 256

.. items = Array'Item'ArenaBacking(arena, capacity)

────────────────────
+ get mark ScratchMark

length

────────────────────
+ do push
    - item Item

if length == items.length
    grow(length + 1)
items[length] = item
length += 1

────────────────────
+ do insert
    - item Item
    - index Index

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch insert index $index out of range")
    if index > length

if length == items.length
    grow(length + 1)
. position = length
while position > index
    items[position] = items[position - 1]
    position -= 1
items[index] = item
length += 1

────────────────────
+ do rewind
    - mark ScratchMark

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch mark $mark out of range")
    if mark > length

length = mark

────────────────────
+ this[index Index]

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch index $index out of range")
    if index >= length

items[index]

────────────────────
+ do this[index Index] = item Item

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch index $index out of range")
    if index >= length

items[index] = item

────────────────────
+ since ImmutableArray'Item'ArenaBacking
    - mark ScratchMark

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch mark $mark out of range")
    if mark > length

items[mark .. < length].immutable

────────────────────
+ span ImmutableArray'Item'ArenaBacking
    - start Size
    - count Size

?! OutOfBoundsError("Scratch span $start+$count out of range")
    if start + count > length

items[start .. < start + count].immutable

────────────────────
_ do grow
    - needed Size

. capacity = items.length * 2
if capacity < 8
    capacity = 8
while capacity < needed
    capacity *= 2
items = items.resize(capacity, arena)
